Code from other projects
------------------------

SSH Pilot (https://github.com/mfat/sshpilot), GPL-3.0-or-later.
  The pseudo-terminal adapter (src/gtk-ghostty-pty.c) is ported from SSH
  Pilot's sshpilot/platform/windows/conpty.py and sshpilot/local_shell_pty.py.
  Code taken from SSH Pilot later (for example its libghostty-vt build script,
  packaging/windows/libghostty-vt/build.py) falls under the same grant. All of
  that code was written by SSH Pilot's author, who is also gtkghostty's
  author, and who on 2026-11-15 relicensed it for gtkghostty under
  LGPL-2.1-or-later. SSH Pilot itself remains GPL-3.0-or-later (meson.build).

tilix2 (https://github.com/markuman/tilix2) at 65d775b, WTFPL v2.
  The key map and the box-drawing/block-element tables (tools/gen_tables.py,
  src/gtk-ghostty-tables.c) and the row drawing scheme in
  src/gtk-ghostty-terminal.c (runs of same-styled cells, letter spacing to the
  cell grid, wide cells scaled to two cells, box drawing on the grid) are
  ported from tilix2.py.

Design references (no code copied)
----------------------------------

Kwi (https://invent.kde.org/utilities/kwi, mirror https://github.com/KDE/kwi)
  at f2810b4, LGPL-2.1-only OR LGPL-3.0-only OR LicenseRef-KDE-Accepted-LGPL.
  The input-method preedit layout follows the design of Kwi's
  PreeditLayout.cpp, and its tests follow the cases in imetest.cpp. The
  set of characters drawn on the cell grid (Powerline, braille, sextants)
  follows the scope of Kwi's Symbols.cpp; the drawing code is original.
  Kwi's code is C++/Qt and is not copied; its licence differs from
  gtkghostty's "or later", so it is used as a design reference only.

Ghostling (https://github.com/ghostty-org/ghostling) at 63842bf, MIT.
  The list of terminal effects to answer (size, XTVERSION, colour scheme).

